# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   See https://github.com/pyenv/pyenv/header#shared-local-path-file
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#599, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in git.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if well-established development environments are used,
#   it may be shared.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock contains the resolved dependencies
#   which should be committed to git.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock contains the resolved dependencies
#   which should be committed to git.
#pdm.lock

